000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.   TDATECHK.
000400*REMARKS.
000500*D   THIS IS A DATE UTILITY PROGRAM THAT WILL AID CALLING PROGRAMS
000600*D   IN FORMATTING DATES IN EITHER AMERICAN OR EUROPEAN STYLE.
000700*
000800*    HOW TO USE THIS SUBPROGRAM:
000900*        IN MODE 0, FIRST DETERMINE THE DATE CODE (EITHER 1 OR 3).
001000*        THEN ADD 3 IF GOING BETWEEN DISPLAY AND DATABASE DATES,
001100*        ADD 6 IF BETWEEN SYSTEM AND DATABASE DATES, OR LEAVE ALONE
001200*        IF GOING BETWEEN SYSTEM AND DISPLAY DATES.  THEN THE
001300*        SUBPROGRAM WILL SIMPLY FLIP MONTH AND DAY IF ITS A
001400*        EUROPEAN PLANT AND IF YOU ADDED 0 OR 3 TO THE DATE CODE.
001500*
001600*        MODE 1 IS USED TO OBTAIN THE CURRENT DATE AND TIME IN THE
001700*        CORRECT STYLE FOR OUTPUT ON DOCUMENTS, SCREENS, REPORTS,
001800*        AND FOR UPDATING THE DATABASE.  (DATABASE FORMAT IS THE
001900*        SAME - YYMMDD - FOR EUROPEAN OR AMERICAN PLANTS).
002000*        IN MODE 1, JUST CALL THE PROGRAM AND THE CURRENT DATE
002100*        AND TIME WILL BE RETURNED IN VARIOUS FORMATS.  THEN
002200*        USE THE FORMAT YOU NEED.  IF ITS A EUROPEAN PLANT,
002300*        THE FORMATTED DATES WILL REFLECT THIS.
002400*
002500*        MODE 2 IS USED TO CONVERT A GIVEN SYSTEM DATE INTO
002600*        VARIOUS FORMATS IN THE CORRECT STYLE.
002700*        IN MODE 2, PASS THE SYSTEM DATE ("CURRENT-DATE").
002800*        IT WILL BE CONVERTED TO VARIOUS FORMATS IN THE
002900*        CORRECT DATE STYLE (AMERICAN OR EUROPEAN).  THEN
003000*        USE THE FORMAT YOU NEED.
003100*
003200*        MODE 3 IS USED TO VALIDATE A DATE INPUTTED FROM A SCREEN,
003300*        AND CONVERT IT TO DATABASE FORMAT.
003400*        IN MODE 3, PASS A DISPLAY DATE INPUTTED FROM A SCREEN.
003500*        IN A EUROPEAN PLANT, THE USER WILL INPUT THE DATE AS
003600*        DAY, THEN MONTH, THEN YEAR.  IN AN AMERICAN PLANT, THE
003700*        USER WILL INPUT THE DATE AS MONTH, THEN DAY, THEN YEAR.
003800*        THE DATE CAN BE PASSED IN ANY FORMAT (IE. FOR AMERICAN,
003900*        THE DATE COULD BE 3/23/85 OR MARCH 3 85 OR MAR 23/85,
004000*        ETC).  THIS DATE WILL THEN BE VALIDATED.  IF THE DATE IS
004100*        INVALID, A RETURN CODE OF 1 WILL BE RETURNED, AND THE
004200*        MESSAGE (I.E. The field must be a valid date...) WILL
004300*        WILL BE RETURNED.  IF THE DATE IS VALID, IT WILL BE
004400*        CONVERTED INTO VARIOUS FORMATS OF THE CORRECT STYLE.
004500*        THEN USE ANY OF THESE CONVERTED DATES THAT YOU NEED.
004600*
004700*        MODE 4 IS USED TO TAKE A DATE FROM THE DATABASE AND
004800*        TRANSFORM IT INTO FORMATS READABLE BY THE USER.
004900*        SIMPLY PASS A DATABASE DATE IN YYMMDD FORMAT, AND IT
005000*        WILL BE RETURNED IN USER FORMATS OF THE CORRECT STYLE.
005100*
005200*    THE PARAMETERS HAVE THE FOLLOWING MEANINGS:
005300*
005400*    DATE-CODE     -  CAN BE EITHER 1, 3, OR 0.
005500*
005600*      1  DATE STYLE IS AMERICAN (MMDDYY)
005700*
005800*      3  DATE STYLE IS EUROPEAN (DDMMYY)
005900*
006000*      0  NO DATE CODE IS PASSED.  IN THIS CASE THE SUBPROGRAM
006100*         WILL DETERMINE THE DATE CODE FROM THE FILE "DDATECOD",
006200*         AND RETURN IT TO THE CALLING PROGRAM. IN THIS CASE ON
006300*         THE SECOND AND ALL FOLLOWING CALLS TO THE SUBPROGRAM,
006400*         THE DATE CODE WILL NOT HAVE TO BE DETERMINED.
006500*         IF THE FILE "DDATECOD" DOES NOT EXIST, THE DEFAULT CODE
006600*         WILL BE 1.
006700*
006800*    THE SUBPROGRAM CAN BE CALLED IN VARIOUS MODES, AS
006900*    FOLLOWS:
007000*
007100*    0  EITHER SYSTEM DATE OR DISPLAY DATE IS PASSED IN X(6) FORMAT
007200*       EITHER DISPLAY DATE OR DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED IN X(6)
007300*       AND ONE OF THE FOLLOWING NUMBERS IS ADDED TO "DATE-CODE"
007400*       TO SPECIFY:
007500*         0  SYSTEM DATE PASSED, DISPLAY DATE RETURNED
007600*            -  SYSTEM DATE PASSED MMDDYY
007700*            -  DISPLAY DATE RETURNED MMDDYY IF AMERICAN
007800*            -  DISPLAY DATE RETURNED DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN
007900*
008000*         3  DISPLAY DATE PASSED, DATABASE DATE RETURNED
008100*            -  DISPLAY DATE PASSED MMDDYYY IF AMERICAN
008200*            -  DISPLAY DATE PASSED DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN
008300*            -  DATABASE DATE RETURNED MMDDYY
008400*
008500*        6  SYSTEM DATE PASSED, DATABASE DATE RETURNED
008600*           -  SYSTEM DATE PASSED MMDDYY
008700*           -  DATABASE DATE RETURNED MMDDYY
008800*
008900*    1  NO DATE IS PASSED
009000*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
009100*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
009200*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
009300*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
009400*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
009500*            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
009600*       c. DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT".
009700*       d. FORMATTED TIME IS RETURNED IN "FORMATTED-TIME-OUT"
009800*            -  HH:MN:SS FORMAT
009900*       e. UNFORMATTED TIME IS RETURNED IN "UNFORMATTED-TIME-OUT"
010000*            -  HHMNSS FORMAT
010100*
010200*    2  SYSTEM DATE IS PASSED (MM/DD/YY) IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN"
010300*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
010400*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
010500*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
010600*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
010700*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
010800*            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
010900*       c. DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT".
011000*
011100*    3  DISPLAY DATE FROM SCREEN IS PASSED IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN".
011200*         -  MONTH, DAY, YEAR IF AMERICAN STYLE
011300*         -  DAY, MONTH, YEAR IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
011400*         -  THE DATE CAN BE IN ANY FORMAT (I.E. FOR EUROPEAN,
011500*            5 JAN 85, 05 JANUARY 85, OR 050185 WOULD BE VALID).
011600*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
011700*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
011800*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
011900*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
012000*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
012100*            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
012200*       c. DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT".
012300*       d. A 1 IS RETURNED IN "DATE-RET-CODE" IF THE DATE IS
012400*          INVALID.
012500*       e. AN ERROR MESSAGE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-MSG" IF THE DATE
012600*          IS INVALID.
012700*
012800*    4  DATABASE DATE IS PASSED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN"
012900*       a. FORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
013000*            -  MM/DD/YY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
013100*            -  DD/MM/YY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
013200*       b. UNFORMATTED DISPLAY DATE IS RETURNED IN "DATE-OUT"
013300*            -  MMDDYY IF AMERICAN STYLE PLANT
013400*            -  DDMMYY IF EUROPEAN STYLE PLANT
013500*       c.  DATABASE DATE IS RETURNED AS YYMMDD IN "DATE-YMD-OUT".
013600*           (THIS DUPLICATES WHAT WAS INPUT IN "DATE-VALIDATE-IN").
013700*
013800*****************
013900** CHANGES     **
014000*****************
014100*
014200*    03/04/86.
014300*        CHANGED THE WAY THIS SUBPROGRAM HANDLES THE SITUATION
014400*        IN MODE 3 (USER DATE) IF A DATE OF SPACES IS PASSED.
014500*        PREVIOUSLY, THE DATE WOULD BE FLAGGED AS INVALID.
014600*        NOW, WILL GIVE A GOOD RETURN CODE, BUT WILL RETURN
014700*        SPACES IN THE VARIOUS DATE FIELDS.  THIS IS TO AVOID
014800*        THE FOLLOWING TYPE OF LOGIC IN THE CALLING PROGRAMS:
014900*          IF DATA-ENTRY-DATE = SPACES
015000*              MOVE SPACES         TO  DATABASE-DATE
015100*          ELSE
015200*              MOVE DATA-ENTRY-DATE TO DATE-VALIDATE-IN
015300*              CALL "TDATECHK"............
015400*        CIH.
015500*
015600*    03/07/86
015700*      CHANGED PROGRAM FOR MODE 4 - IF THE DATABASE DATE
015800*      IS SPACES, RETURNS SPACES IN "DATE-SLASH-OUT"
015900*      INSTEAD OF "  /  /  ".  CIH.
016000*
016000*    11/23/93      BK DISMUKES
016000*      ADDED LOGIC TO RECOGNIZE EUROPEAN DATE FORMAT.
016000*
016100 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
016200 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
016300 SOURCE-COMPUTER. AS-400.
016400 OBJECT-COMPUTER. AS-400.
016500*SPECIAL-NAMES.
016600*    CONDITION-CODE IS C-C.
016700 DATA DIVISION.
016800 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
016900 01  SAVE-AREA                     PIC X(2).
017000 01  DATE-WORK.
017100     05  DATE-WORK-MD              PIC 9(2).
017200     05  DATE-WORK-DM              PIC 9(2).
017300     05  DATE-WORK-YY              PIC 9(2).
017400 01  LEAP-YEAR-FLAG                PIC X(1)  VALUE "N".
017500 01  LEAP-TEST                     PIC 9(4)V9(4).
017600 01  LEAP-REDEF REDEFINES LEAP-TEST.
017700     05  FILLER                    PIC 9(4).
017800     05  LEAP-TEST-DEC             PIC 9(4).
017900
       01  IBM-DATE-WORK.
           05  IBM-DATE-WORK-YY PIC X(2).
           05  IBM-DATE-WORK-MM PIC X(2).
           05  IBM-DATE-WORK-DD PIC X(2).
018000
018100 01  DDATECOD-FILE  PIC X(22) VALUE "DDATECOD/DONTPURG.PUB".
018200 01  DDATECOD-FNUM  PIC S9(4) COMP-4 VALUE 0.
018300
018300 COPY CCHKOBJ   IN  COPYLIB.
018300
018400 LINKAGE SECTION.
018500 01  DATE-CHECK-AREA.
018600     05  DATE-CODE                 PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
018700     05  DATE-MODE                 PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
018800     05  DATE-IN.
018900         10  DATE-IN-MD            PIC X(2).
019000         10  DATE-IN-DM            PIC X(2).
019100         10  DATE-IN-YY            PIC X(2).
019200     05  DATE-OUT.
019300         10  DATE-OUT-MD           PIC X(2).
019400         10  DATE-OUT-DM           PIC X(2).
019500         10  DATE-OUT-YY           PIC X(2).
019600     05  DATE-RET-CODE             PIC S9(4) COMP-4.
019700     05  DATE-VALIDATE-IN          PIC X(20).
019800*----- DATE TYPE EXAMPLES
019900*----- DATE-TYPE-0             030585
020000*----- DATE-TYPE-1             03/05/85
020100*----- DATE-TYPE-2             03/5/85
020200*----- DATE-TYPE-3             3/05/85
020300*----- DATE-TYPE-4             3/5/85
020400     05  DATE-TYPE-0 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
020500         10  DATE-NUMERIC          PIC X(6).
020600         10  FILLER                PIC X(14).
020700     05  DATE-TYPE-1 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
020800         10  DT1-MD                PIC X(2).
020900         10  DT1-S1                PIC X(1).
021000         10  DT1-DM                PIC X(2).
021100         10  DT1-S2                PIC X(1).
021200         10  DT1-YY                PIC X(2).
021300         10  FILLER                PIC X(12).
021400     05  DATE-TYPE-2 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
021500         10  DT2-MD                PIC X(2).
021600         10  DT2-S1                PIC X(1).
021700         10  DT2-DM                PIC X(1).
021800         10  DT2-S2                PIC X(1).
021900         10  DT2-YY                PIC X(2).
022000         10  FILLER                PIC X(13).
022100     05  DATE-TYPE-3 REDEFINES DATE-VALIDATE-IN.
022200         10  DT3-MD                PIC X(1).
